{"seq":12,"trial_id":"harness-zero-h2h-2026-11/openclaw-opus-none-mu-v03-dev2/sy-01-quarrendon-ticket-numbers/r4","wall_ts":"2026-11-07T10:03:45.690Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-14T09:10:00-05:00","args_digest":"545ff85aafa894486c9538203474511b82db729893acc359e3fd251fbabd5058","actor":"assistant","via":"mcp","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"DHARNES0001","text":"Hi Hollis. I went through all of Moss's notes in the shared files. Two of them give ticket numbers for Quarrendon Freight Lines:\n\n• *#PD-4492*, from Moss's \"Sunday prep for Ruth\" digest dated 5 Oct 2025 (teams/team-north/digests/2025-10-05-north-sunday.md). Thea Ramaswell logged it on 4 Oct 2025 because drivers at Dock Doors 14–18 in the Eau Claire yard weren't getting SMS bay assignments at gatehouse check-in. Support patched it that evening, and Thea confirmed it was fixed on 5 Oct.\n• *#4419*, from Moss's undated \"North cheat sheet\" (teams/team-north/digests/north-account-cheatsheet.md). Thea logged it because gatehouse barcode scanners weren't reading trailer tags at Door 14 on third shift. It was escalated to tier-2 product support for scanner firmware testing.\n\nThings I left out:\n• #4409, #4412 and FR-882 in Moss's Central handoffs digest belong to Pree's dealer account and Marrow Agrisupply, not QFL.\n• Moss's 14 Sep 2025 North pipeline digest and 23 Mar 2026 renewal check-in both mention QFL but don't give any ticket numbers.\n• Marcus's \"Quarendon Freightways\" note (one r) is about a different company that isn't a customer.\n\nThis only covers what's in Moss's notes. QFL's own ticket records may have more."},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"DHARNES0001","ts":"1791987000.000124"}}
{"seq":13,"trial_id":"harness-zero-h2h-2026-11/openclaw-opus-none-mu-v03-dev2/sy-01-quarrendon-ticket-numbers/r4","wall_ts":"2026-11-07T10:03:51.826Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-14T09:10:00-05:00","args_digest":"0a9ab6f6aa4fded5149365c751c3688ae172e58f71410086fdf51eda41b59545","actor":"assistant","via":"slack","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"DHARNES0001","text":"I found two Quarrendon Freight Lines ticket numbers in Moss's notes and sent you the list in our DM:\n\n- **#PD-4492:** comes from Moss's \"Sunday prep for Ruth\" digest dated 5 Oct 2025. Drivers at Dock Doors 14–18 in the Eau Claire yard weren't getting their dock assignments by text when they checked in. Support fixed it on 4 Oct, and Thea Ramaswell confirmed the fix on 5 Oct.\n- **#4419:** comes from Moss's undated \"North cheat sheet.\" Barcode scanners at the gatehouse weren't reading trailer tags at Door 14 on third shift. It was passed to second-level product support to test the scanner firmware.\n\nI left these out:\n- **#4409, #4412 and FR-882:** these are in Moss's Central handoffs digest, but they belong to Pree's dealer account and Marrow Agrisupply, not Quarrendon.\n- **Two other Moss notes:** the 14 Sep 2025 North pipeline digest and the 23 Mar 2026 renewal check-in mention Quarrendon but give no ticket numbers.\n- **Marcus's \"Quarendon Freightways\" note:** that's a different company (one \"r\") and not a customer.\n\nI only searched Moss's notes in the shared files, which you can open yourself. Quarrendon's own ticket records may list more tickets."},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"DHARNES0001","ts":"1791987000.000125"}}
